    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting an elite efficiency score of 80.98, he is the primary engine for our scarcity-driven strategy; his leadoff role against a favorable 4.77 xERA matchup, combined with a 100% stolen base expectation against the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery, makes him an essential start. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** also presents significant value at 68.40. His matchup against Lopez is bolstered by a +10% park factor and +18% SP skill edge, creating a prime environment for power production. Conversely, we are exercising caution with **Dillon Dingler**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Chase Meidroth**, all of whom face elite-tier arms with xERAs below 3.00, suppressing their scores into the marginal 42\u201348 range.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Carson Benge**, whose score of 59.08 was respectable but ultimately fell short of our efficiency threshold compared to the high-ceiling alternatives in our outfield. While **Carson Benge** offers strong platoon and order advantages, he lacked the explosive stolen base upside inherent in the profiles of our active starters. We are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Dillon Dingler**, who must navigate a high-difficulty start against Skubal; despite his favorable platoon split, the pitcher's elite skill makes this a defensive start rather than an offensive one. We remain hopeful for production from **Junior Caminero** and **Yordan Alvarez**, both of whom maintain strong scores despite challenging park factors, as their elite skill levels and high-leadoff positioning in the order provide a necessary buffer against volatility.",
